Serializer API works with:

- primitive types: int, float, string, bool, vector
- dynamic containers: array, set, map
- static arrays
- complex types: classes

**Note:** Serializer provides deep serialization (it serialize class memebers and their members etc). To avoid serialization of certain class variable, use NonSerialized attribute.

Usage:

```
class MyData
{
    int m_id;
    map<string, float> m_values;

    [NonSerialized()]
    string m_dbg; // I don't want to serialize this variable
}

void Serialize(Serializer s)
{
    int statArray[4] = {6,9,2,3};
    array<int> dynArray = {8,5,6,4};
    MyData data = new MyData();

    data.m_id = 965;
    data.m_values = map<string, float>;
    data.m_values.Insert("value1", 5.98);
    data.m_values.Insert("value2", 4.36);

    s.Write(10);
    s.Write("Hello");
    s.Write(statArray);
    s.Write(dynArray);
    s.Write(data);
}

void Deserialize(Serializer s)
{
    int statArray[4];
    array<int> dynArray;
    MyData data;
    int someInt;
    string someString;

    s.Read(someInt);
    s.Read(someString);
    s.Read(statArray);
    s.Read(dynArray);
    s.Read(data);
}
```

staticMethods.description:
Request creation of a new ban.

Fill in the manifest with the target, scope action, reason and duration before calling.

The resulting BanEntry is stored inside the callback and deleted alongside it. Retrieve via BackendCallback.GetResultData() cast to BanEntry.

API codes delivered to the callback:

- OnSuccess - ban was created. Retrieve the created BanEntry via BackendCallback.GetResultData() cast to BanEntry.
- OnError:
  - EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_DUPLICATE_BAN - a ban for this target already exists in the specified ban list. The existing BanEntry is also available via BackendCallback.GetResultData() cast to BanEntry.

```
ref BackendCallback m_CreateBanCallback;

void CreateBan(ServerBanManifest manifest)
{
    m_CreateBanCallback = new BackendCallback();
    m_CreateBanCallback.SetOnSuccess(OnCreateBanSuccess);
    m_CreateBanCallback.SetOnError(OnCreateBanError);
    ServerBanManagerApi.RequestCreateBan(m_CreateBanCallback, manifest);
}

void OnCreateBanSuccess(BackendCallback callback)
{
    BanEntry ban = BanEntry.Cast(callback.GetResultData());
    // use the newly created ban entry
}

void OnCreateBanError(BackendCallback callback)
{
    if (callback.GetApiCode() == EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_DUPLICATE_BAN)
    {
        BanEntry existing = BanEntry.Cast(callback.GetResultData());
        // a ban for this target already exists - existing holds the duplicate entry
    }
}
```

methods.description:
Requests to join this server.

The server will either approve the join immediately or place the user in a queue if the server is full.

Before calling, ensure the server IsJoinable(), supports the client platform (IsMyPlatformSupported()), and has the password set via SetPassword() if the server IsPasswordProtected().

**Parameters:**

|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| callback | Receives the result of the join request. |
| onDetails | Optional function invoked when full server details are received, before the join completes. Use this to perform final validations (e.g. checking connected players). To cancel the join from inside this function, set the callback to null. |

**Exceptions:**

|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| VME | If the server is not joinable, does not support the client platform, requires a password that was not set, or another request for this server is already in progress. |

API codes delivered to the callback:

- OnSuccess:
  - EApiCode.EACODE_SERVER_JOIN — join approved, request a game state transition to connect to the server.
  - EApiCode.EACODE_SERVER_QUEUE_WAIT — the user was placed in a queue or entered UNREADY limbo. Occurs when the server is full (user is queued), or when the user joined with BUSY status while a slot was available (UNREADY state). Use ServerJoinManagerApi.GetQueueData() to access queue info and set up a polling callback for status updates.
- OnError:
  - EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_SERVER_NOT_FOUND — server no longer exists.
  - EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_SERVER_PASSWORD_MISMATCH — incorrect password.
  - EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_SERVER_IS_FULL — server is full and has no queue.
  - EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_SERVER_JOIN_UNREADY_DENIED — the user attempted to join with BUSY status but the server does not have a queue enabled. Transition to READY via ServerJoinManagerApi::SetUserStatus(true) and retry.
  - EApiCode.EACODE_ERROR_PLAYER_IS_BANNED — the local player is banned from this server. Use ServerJoinManagerApi.GetLastJoinBanEntry() to retrieve the ban details (scope, reason, expiry).

**See also:** ServerJoinManagerApi

**See also:** ServerQueueData

```
ref BackendCallback joinCallback;
ServerInfo serverToJoin;

// Simple join
void Join()
{
    serverToJoin.RequestJoin(joinCallback);
}

// Join with pre-join validation
void JoinWithValidation()
{
    serverToJoin.RequestJoin(joinCallback, OnDetailsReceived);
}

// Called when server details are received, before join completes
void OnDetailsReceived()
{
    // perform any checks, e.g. blocked players

    if (shouldCancel)
    {
        joinCallback = null; // cancels the join
    }

    // returning without nulling the callback continues the join
}

// Handle callback result
void OnJoinResult(BackendCallback callback)
{
    EApiCode result = callback.GetApiCode();

    if (result == EApiCode.EACODE_SERVER_JOIN)
    {
        // approved — request game state transition to connect
    }
    else if (result == EApiCode.EACODE_SERVER_QUEUE_WAIT)
    {
        // placed in queue — set up polling callback for updates
        ServerQueueData queueData = ServerJoinManagerApi.GetQueueData();
        queueData.SetPollingCallback(joinCallback);
    }
}
```

